---
import { useTranslations, getLangFromUrl } from '@/i18n/utils'
const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url)
const t = useTranslations(lang)
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'


import HeadingTextBlock from '../organisms/heading-text-block.astro'
---


<Layout title='About' heading="ABOUT ME" subHeading="few of the things that made me the way i am">
	<p>
		Before I even knew terms like layout or design, I was fascinated by
		magazines and fanzines - especially those focused on music. It wasn’t just
		the content that drew me in, but also the form: the way text, photography,
		and graphics come together to create a cohesive whole. As a teenager, I
		tried to create my own fanzine. Today I cringe a little thinking about its
		imperfections, but the satisfaction of putting it together was very real -
		and, in many ways, that hasn’t changed. Years later, I found the same
		satisfaction in translating the language of
		design into code. 
	</p>

	<HeadingTextBlock headingText='hobbies'>
		<p>{t('about.hobbies')}</p>
	</HeadingTextBlock>
	<HeadingTextBlock headingText='music'>
		<p>{t('about.music')}</p>
	</HeadingTextBlock>
	<HeadingTextBlock headingText='film'>
		<p>{t('about.film')}</p>
	</HeadingTextBlock>
</Layout>
